{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379527-exalts-with-dependents","id":1379527,"title":"Exalts with dependents?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-08T15:09:56-07:00","id":1379527,"title":"Exalts with dependents?","content":"So ignoring the fact that you aren't part of a big organisation. You aren't a dynast, you aren't a member of the silver pact, or whatnot. You're just... some guy who exalted in the middle of nowhere. No support network. No assistants. Maybe you exalted as a solar when you built a mechanical harvester to help your father's aging back, or you survived killing a tyrant lizard. Or its your 18th birthday, and you become a dragonblooded. <br /> <br /> So you've got parents, children, younger siblings, or whatever. Basically, you got them with you, and you gotta stay with them. What do you do? Do you bring them along with you? Do you just stay put and hunker down? <br /> <br /> If so, then what adventures do you write? The story of 'how we made a spring and made a water pump', or do you write a story of problems coming to them, what with the myraid dangers a village in the age of sorrows experiences?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T15:41:34-07:00","id":1379531,"title":"","content":"I'm reminded of an old greentext story which I don't seem to have on-hand about a town guard being offered to become a PC... and this: <a href=\"https://www.handbookofheroes.com/archives/comic/the-handbook-of-heroes-13\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.handbookofheroes.com/arc...k-of-heroes-13</a><br /> <br /> But more seriously:<br /> <br /> My characters are often Dynasts (lots of dependents, big support network), Alchemicals (no dependents, big support network) or Infernals (I ate my dependents, big support network).<br /> <br /> But the Solars I've played with kids kinda played out like Goku and his kids. I was pretty damn negilgent.<br /> <br /> I see a lot of room for Lone Wolf and Cub style stories. And I also see a lot of scope for the traveling Exalt who leaves their family somewhere safe(ish), like Whitewall, and comes home between adventures to marvel at how their kids have grown.<br /> <br /> I say go full Age of Sorrows... but then I'm used to Ward being a 3-point flaw. I guess it's a Session 0 thing?<br /> <br /> My only 3E character is going to have a newborn soon (once we stop playing flashbacks... hmm... there's a thought, we could flashback to the birth of our now adult children). But they're a Dynast couple living with their two adult children, mortal allies, brother and wife and nephew, sister, aunt and cousin. &quot;Watch the baby, brb -- gotta kick ass&quot; is pretty much the order of the day here.<br /> <br /> Superhero comics have high action, and Marvel leans into a family focus. Not exactly the right genre, but that might give you some ideas. How much page time did Squirrel Girl get looking after Luke and Jessica's baby? I only remember a couple of panels from Secret Invasion, but that's probably got some ripe fodder. And Fantastic Four with the twins. And, you know, go immediately read all of Lone Wolf and Cub.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T16:32:03-07:00","id":1379546,"title":"","content":"And another thing. When you get a younger brother, or when your solar twilight medicine herbalist has 2 sons she has to bring around with her due to the wyld hunt.... well, how does she deal with them? Set loose an army of demons to serve as guards? Hit up other people for alliance and help? Bring them along with her because she's probably the deadliest combatant for miles around despite the fact that this brings them right into the line of fire? <br /> <br /> Just questions to think about. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T16:36:16-07:00","id":1379547,"title":"","content":"Yeah <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar531_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"531\" data-vbnamecard=\"531\">JohnDoe244</a> , I was more thinking of the various shit that comes around when you play 'wandering mercenary' and you have a younger sister or son with you. Changes a lot of things. Like the possible amounts of trauma she gets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T16:36:42-07:00","id":1379548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379527-exalts-with-dependents?p=1379531#post1379531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the Solars I've played with kids kinda played out like Goku and his kids. I was pretty damn negilgent.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Your dad is dead! For good!&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200b&quot;But he just got back from his training. After getting back from Namek. After getting back from his training. AFTER BEING DEAD.\u200b&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200b&quot;Bye son~!&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T18:47:53-07:00","id":1379566,"title":"","content":"Must... not... correct memes... actually interesting topic at hand!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379527-exalts-with-dependents?p=1379546#post1379546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And another thing. When you get a younger brother, or when your solar twilight medicine herbalist has 2 sons she has to bring around with her due to the wyld hunt.... well, how does she deal with them? Set loose an army of demons to serve as guards? <b>Hit up other people for alliance and help?</b> Bring them along with her because she's probably the deadliest combatant for miles around despite the fact that this brings them right into the line of fire?</div> </div> </div> </div>That one in particular... I think in a lot of examples of the kinds of circumstances you're describing, people will be in an instance where community is pretty close knit. There may have been many other circumstances in which neighbours who have essentially functioned as godparents need to graduate to full parents now that you understandably need to go on the run. So long as you're not leaving behind any enemies who might out them, well... it's probably not beyond the capabilities of the Wyld Hunt to sufficiently interrogate residents for the identities of anybody who might serve as leverage against the Anathema, but I'd find it credible that many will not care to risk wasting the time while their quarry continues to get a lead. Not unless they've at least got a lead that the target left family behind.<br /> <br /> Which is not to say that taking them with you should not be done, but that it raises questions about what kind of compelling drama was behind <i>why</i> it was done. Do you have an enemy in your community that would expose them for malice or opportunity? Do you have an overriding personal need to keep your children with you even if it might be pragmatically safer to leave them behind?<br /> <br /> Suddenly I'm imagining an Exalt whose personal demeanour was not so inclined towards the acquisition of lands, property and titles (really more of an artistic or creative type), but feels compelled to do so and become caught up in schemes of dynastic matchmaking because hey, your kids grew up resenting the fact that you uprooted their lives and carried them off into uncertainty and danger for lacking the will to be separated from them, and you're not really sure what to do to avoid having to watch them grow old hating you besides trying to buy back their love. Annnd maybe at least one of them was kind of an asshole and actively capitalised on that anxiety because, you know, having a parent capable and motivated to get you that shit is an astronomically rare opportunity.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T19:20:08-07:00","id":1379575,"title":"","content":"Wait. Why do you think there should be an overarching need for them to *not* bring their children along? For starters, no parent would really want to be separated from their child. Also, there could be fear of alienation. Farming communities, at least as I understand them in the old days (apologies for the generalization) are xenophobic, insular, and hell for those who are ostracised. Do you really want your kids to grow up as 'The kids of the woman who turned Anathema'? They could be ostracized, shunned, starved, or even banished or sold as slaves because who would want to be associated with them? And also, leaving your kids behind means that there's the chance that they'll be used as leverage. You want to trust them to be left to the tender 'mercies' of the dragonblooded?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T19:50:55-07:00","id":1379584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379527-exalts-with-dependents?p=1379566#post1379566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Suddenly I'm imagining an Exalt whose personal demeanour was not so inclined towards the acquisition of lands, property and titles (really more of an artistic or creative type), but feels compelled to do so and become caught up in schemes of dynastic matchmaking because hey, your kids grew up resenting the fact that you uprooted their lives and carried them off into uncertainty and danger for lacking the will to be separated from them, and you're not really sure what to do to avoid having to watch them grow old hating you besides trying to buy back their love. Annnd maybe at least one of them was kind of an asshole and actively capitalised on that anxiety because, you know, having a parent capable and motivated to get you that shit is an astronomically rare opportunity.</div> </div> </div> </div>So what you're saying is that the children of Exalted are basically like... the children of the Noveau Riche, only with lots and lots of superpowers instead of money? Wonder how the parties are like....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T19:52:25-07:00","id":1379587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379527-exalts-with-dependents?p=1379575#post1379575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do you think there should be an overarching need for them to *not* bring their children along?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it's dangerous, or unfair.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">For starters, no parent would really want to be separated from their child.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is incorrect. So many parents want to be separated from their children, a heartbreaking number. I have personally in real life known no less than three people who had a parent that walked out on them. In the grand scheme of things, that can actually be the best outcome for a a child whose patent wants to be shot of them.<br /> <br /> It is also irrelevant. There are numerous circumstances in which a parent is required to spend great lengths of time away from children that they do want to be around, a heartbreaking number. I myself have a cousin who works on an oil rig, no place for his children is that, and there are several other professions with similar constraints, or other life circumstances that force such a thing. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, there could be fear of alienation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also a source of compelling drama.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Farming communities, at least as I understand them in the old days (apologies for the generalization) are xenophobic, insular, and hell for those who are ostracised. Do you really want your kids to grow up as 'The kids of the woman who turned Anathema'? They could be ostracized, shunned, starved, or even banished or sold as slaves because who would want to be associated with them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Obviously I described a scenario in which the Exalt is not an outsider. Even in circumstances where a neighbor whom you might trust children with would be against you as Anathema, they might still care for the children enough to not want them caught in the crossfire.<br /> <br /> Jeez, don't bring up that families can be left in the care of allies and follow up with a dispute when I point out allies that they could be left with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And also, leaving your kids behind means that there's the chance that they'll be used as leverage. <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Taking them with you means that there's the chance that they'll be standing between you and an elemental bolt. Calculated risks abound.<br /> <br /> Never mind the fact that I addressed this subject in the actual post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T21:19:20-07:00","id":1379594,"title":"","content":"<b>Re: Dependents</b><br /> <br /> For a story that center's around the Exalt and their relationships with their dependents, it is hard to make over-arching generalities. Each character is going to approach these decisions differently, and how they approach them will become things that define who the character is and what will be the most interesting stories to tell.<br /> <br /> Ask what the decision to take your kids with you on your adventures (or leave them at home) says about the character. I would even make sure the dependents have their own personality and ideas, if only to create interactions with more verisimilitude.<br /> <br /> I would recommend a strong blend of bitter and sweet. If the dependent is just a target for every enemy, then the player (not the character) will start making characters that don't have any real attachments. And I consider attachments are a big part of what makes Exalted work (at least for me). Too much sweet, and a real sense of tension is lost, and tension makes for better stories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T23:38:29-07:00","id":1379657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379527-exalts-with-dependents?p=1379547#post1379547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar531_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"531\" data-vbnamecard=\"531\">JohnDoe244</a> , I was more thinking of the various shit that comes around when you play 'wandering mercenary' and you have a younger sister or son with you. Changes a lot of things. Like the possible amounts of trauma she gets.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I immediately insist you read Lone Wolf and Cub. Or at least watch the 1980 film adaptation &quot;Shogun Assassin&quot;.<br /> <br /> The entire premise is that the Emperor's personal executioner's (the most dangerous warrior in all Japan) wife murdered and he is forced into exile thanks to the political machinations of the Emperor's arch-enemies. He wanders the land as a sword-for-hire, bringing justice to the empire and vengeance upon his enemies in loyal service to an emperor who wants him dead. He kills armies and reinvents warfare...<br /> <br /> ... whilst pushing his infant son around in a baby carriage.<br /> <br /> It is the most Exalted thing I've ever read.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 09-18-2020, 04:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T23:51:57-07:00","id":1379668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379527-exalts-with-dependents?p=1379657#post1379657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I immediately insist you read Lone Wolf and Cub. Or at least watch the 1980 film adaptation &quot;Shogun Assassin&quot;.<br /> <br /> The entire premise is that the Emperor's personal executioner (the most dangerous warrior in all Japan) has his wife murdered and is forced into exile thanks to the political machinations of the Emperor's arch-enemies. He wanders the land as a sword-for-hire, bringing justice to the empire and vengeance upon his enemies in loyal service to an emperor who wants him dead. He kills armies and reinvents warfare...<br /> <br /> ... whilst pushing his infant son around in a baby carriage.<br /> <br /> It is the most Exalted thing I've ever read.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah my mind jumps to that immediately. Or my 2.5 game where a Player layed a golden egg, and the egg hatched a Golden Snakebaby. She was a Lunar Snakewoman in my version of Halta. But she was famous dancer diva so its not quite the same as say being a farmer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T11:43:07-07:00","id":1379821,"title":"","content":"I can imagine a great campaign where you take a random Satrapy, have several people in the satrapy Exalt as various types of Anathema, and they depose the Satrap and kick out the Realm (or at least try to) and then have to deal with keeping the place together while preparing for one of the Houses to send a Legion or two to make a point.<br /> <br /> ...Or maybe they fail and have to run away and become robin hood or something.<br /> <br /> Either way, having each player create two dependents and an enemy would be a great way to add depth and texture and stakes to the whole thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T19:32:56-07:00","id":1379999,"title":"","content":"Four words: Tiger-Warrior Training Technique","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T19:51:40-07:00","id":1380002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379527-exalts-with-dependents?p=1379999#post1379999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Four words: Tiger-Warrior Training Technique</div> </div> </div> </div>Great for battle groups, but doesn't do anything exceptional for individuals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T19:52:44-07:00","id":1380003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379527-exalts-with-dependents?p=1379584#post1379584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what you're saying is that the children of Exalted are basically like... the children of the Noveau Riche, only with lots and lots of superpowers instead of money? Wonder how the parties are like....</div> </div> </div> </div>In a case like this, I don't really think it makes sense to talk about &quot;the Exalted&quot;, so much as &quot;here are parameters, what individual character ideas can you get from it&quot;. There <b>are</b> trends that can be used to describe the Exalted, but I think a subject such as this falls to the point that there are not very many of them and their distribution is a bit arbitrary.<br /> <br /> However, in an instance where the people and motives line up like that, I'd say children of the Nouveau Riche is a fitting analogy.<br /> <br /> Still, your original post did refer to other forms of dependent. What about parents...<br /> <br /> The obvious one is when parents are elderly and one is part of a culture that values caring for them in their golden years, and treasures several generations under one roof. Filiel piety as the initial driving force behind the use of one's powers, that sounds to me like it would make for a very interesting household. You owe so much to that parent and there are only a few short years to make up for it, what shall you do? Stay within a house that under your care becomes ever larger and grander, filled with comfort and beauty. Render it the iron core of an empire (literal or metaphorical) through which you will project the name and reputation of your parents until they have the very status of gods?<br /> <br /> Oh father, I hear legends of a most wondrous peach in the orchards of Heaven that will restore you to the prime of youth. Permit me to go out on a journey of unknown length and obstacles so that I might bring this thing back to you, freeing you of the infirmities of age that you might enjoy a second life without obligations of family while liberating me from the requirement to stay here for the next decade or so caring for and abasing myself before you.<br /> <br /> Just don't go dying before I get back, all right? I don't want to spend the next five hundred years grappling with that lack of closure and sense of guilt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T19:57:13-07:00","id":1380006,"title":"","content":"Good thing there are alchemy that slows down aging and that spell that puts someone in stasis....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T20:25:40-07:00","id":1380011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379527-exalts-with-dependents?p=1380002#post1380002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great for battle groups, but doesn't do anything exceptional for individuals.</div> </div> </div> </div>A family is just a battle group you haven\u2019t trained yet. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T21:08:31-07:00","id":1380020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379527-exalts-with-dependents?p=1380011#post1380011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A family is just a battle group you haven\u2019t trained yet. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>The Incredibles, Exalted edition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T21:13:11-07:00","id":1380021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379527-exalts-with-dependents?p=1380020#post1380020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Incredibles, Exalted edition?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really - the Incredibles had a drastically different set of skills and powers. They're individuals.<br /> <br /> \u200bThink more most of the Crazy 88 from <i>Kill Bill</i> (absent Johnny Mo, the ax-thrower, and the one with the meteor hammer).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-10-2020, 12:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T21:33:52-07:00","id":1380028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379527-exalts-with-dependents?p=1380002#post1380002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great for battle groups, but doesn't do anything exceptional for individuals.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Technically it also upgrades the QC to Battle Ready Troops or Elite Troops.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T23:13:28-07:00","id":1380035,"title":"","content":"In the Chronicle I'm currently in my character has an adolescent son. Early on, he was something to round out my character concept.<br /> <br /> Once we all exalted as Solars and it was getting more difficult to obscure our identities as Solars my character's son has become far more central to her story (and by extension the Circle's story). As a result of a poor choice to fight a Fair Folk cataphract she was left with a derangement (thanks to my GM applying a mental crippling wound rather than a physical one) concerning her son's safety. When the Circle fled their kingdom's Capital (hours before it was invaded by a Prasadan Wyld Hunt) she brought her son along all the while looking for a place of refuge to secret him while the Circle looked to grow stronger, build alliances and power base, and avoid detection by the invading Immaculates.<br /> <br /> Having found a safe haven she left her boy in the care of a village protected by a powerful spirit. The Circle then ventured to Rathess to consolidate their power and collect needed resources to liberate their kingdom. Unbeknownst to my character her business partner in the Rathesian venture hired a sorcerer of some power to protect her son (and partly as leverage over her devouring his soul just in case she actually was a demon infested Anathema). Ultimately, the sorcerer sold her son to a pirate band to settle her business partner's debts.<br /> <br /> Once we concluded our business in Rathess and returned home we discovered these facts and my character was frantic in eking out her son. A little legwork led the Circle to locate and negotiate with the pirate band which had subsumed a number other, smaller bands including the one &quot;protecting&quot; her son. The negotiator was fairly direct and she got her son back but not after he had spent half a year or more in the presence of various unsavoury types and exposed to all manner of bloodthirsty, vicious, violent, and depraved acts.<br /> <br /> All this leaves her with an emotionally scarred child with likely abandonment and separation issues on her hands who is having to also come to terms with the fact that his mother and her friends are Anathema. Set this against the backdrop of keeping a low profile while reinserting into society in the Capital -- a Capital occupied by a foreign army.<br /> <br /> So, yes dependants can drive and enrich stories. You don't have to be a murder hobo to have fun. Even my character having a single dependent (though she has employees too -- followers) makes the story more complex for the three murder hobos in her Circle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11847-kfinigan","name":"KFinigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T23:52:43-07:00","id":1380041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379527-exalts-with-dependents?p=1380028#post1380028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technically it also upgrades the QC to Battle Ready Troops or Elite Troops.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't work on <i>just any</i> QCs though - it specifically enhances Drill, a trait possessed by battle groups.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T00:48:35-07:00","id":1380048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379527-exalts-with-dependents?p=1380002#post1380002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great for battle groups, but doesn't do anything exceptional for individuals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dependent<b><u>s</u></b>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379527-exalts-with-dependents?p=1380003#post1380003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, your original post did refer to other forms of dependent. What about parents...<br /> <br /> The obvious one is when parents are elderly and one is part of a culture that values caring for them in their golden years, and treasures several generations under one roof. </div> </div> </div> </div>I've only seen this in breach: characters forced to abandon their fillial responsibilities as they flee the Wyld Hunt, driven by guilt in their exile, taunted occasionally for their failure to their family, returning home in disgrace to find their beloved parent dead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 04-10-2020, 03:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T00:54:43-07:00","id":1380049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379527-exalts-with-dependents?p=1380048#post1380048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dependent<b><u>s</u></b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, if you have enough dependents that are fairly similar and insignificant enough for the Battle Group rules to look like a good way to represent them, by all means, do so. But most of the times I've featured an Exalt PC's parents in a story, they've been significant enough to have them be individuals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T00:55:24-07:00","id":1380050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379527-exalts-with-dependents?p=1380003#post1380003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Still, your original post did refer to other forms of dependent. What about parents...<br /> <br /> The obvious one is when parents are elderly and one is part of a culture that values caring for them in their golden years, and treasures several generations under one roof. Filiel piety as the initial driving force behind the use of one's powers, that sounds to me like it would make for a very interesting household. You owe so much to that parent and there are only a few short years to make up for it, what shall you do? Stay within a house that under your care becomes ever larger and grander, filled with comfort and beauty. Render it the iron core of an empire (literal or metaphorical) through which you will project the name and reputation of your parents until they have the very status of gods?<br /> <br /> Oh father, I hear legends of a most wondrous peach in the orchards of Heaven that will restore you to the prime of youth. Permit me to go out on a journey of unknown length and obstacles so that I might bring this thing back to you, freeing you of the infirmities of age that you might enjoy a second life without obligations of family while liberating me from the requirement to stay here for the next decade or so caring for and abasing myself before you.<br /> <br /> Just don't go dying before I get back, all right? I don't want to spend the next five hundred years grappling with that lack of closure and sense of guilt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alternatively, you get the celestial bureaucracy to turn him into a god. Or invade the underworld....<br /> <br /> But actually, that wasn't what I had in mind. There's no actual age limit for what a person can exalt as. Even children, rarely, can be exalted. This goes especially highly for Dragonblooded, since its likely they're exalted in their young adult or teenage years. What, then? Conventional marriage during this kind of period means that the parent is, at the lowest possible scale 30 years or so during exaltation. There's a lot of change to get around with. For starters, when the parent tells her child to go to her room, does the child obey or disobey? When she orders her child to, say, do his/ her chores... can the kid get out of it by summoning demons or elementals or the stalwart servitor? <br /> <br /> Suddenly realizing that your daughter or son is an elemental demigod or chosen by the dragons, would mean a hell of a change in terms of discipline. I shudder to think what a teen who just realized that he'd been chosen by the dragons would lead to:<br /> <br /> Someone trying to live up to the expectations he had thrust upon him<br /> <br /> Or someone that's basically let the power go to his head.<br /> <br /> Or if your child turns out to be the Anathema. What happens when its your kid that has to protect you? What happens when you have to see the child you've raised since infancy, look at you with tears in their eyes and a light shining from them? Do they forsake everything they have in their world and go on the run, or do they just sit there and watch as their child disappears into the unknown? When they stroll around and start building an empire, what place do they have for you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T05:20:21-07:00","id":1380091,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379527-exalts-with-dependents?p=1380006#post1380006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good thing there are alchemy that slows down aging and that spell that puts someone in stasis....</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200b</span></span></span></div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Sometimes there is. Hopefully Dad will not pass away while you were seeking out the wizard whom you hoped would ensure he does not pass away while you're going out to find a peach of immortality.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379527-exalts-with-dependents?p=1380050#post1380050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alternatively, you get the celestial bureaucracy to turn him into a god.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you know that that's a thing?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or invade the underworld....</div> </div> </div> </div>Obviously the pathos of that scenario presume that the parent leaves no ghost.<br /> <br /> That said, an alternative path I considered is one in which the Exalted child wishes to go out and acquire a sudden surge of wealth to ensure an appropriately fine funeral to gird their parents for the world below. If they should fail, making a descent to try and strong arm a greater position for them directly is possible, and carries its own dramatic consequences. If a Deathlord or Abyssal reprimands you for such a defiance of the order of the Underworld, selfish and unfair to those who struggled to ensure that their lives would suitably garnish their deaths, are they in the wrong?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But actually, that wasn't what I had in mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you not want to talk about it then?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Conventional marriage during this kind of period means that the parent is, at the lowest possible scale 30 years or so during exaltation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, the idea of particularly young marriages is mostly an ahistorical myth. It seems to be based on an assumption that what was the norm for the upper classes was the norm for everybody (and even that tends to be distorted by a misunderstanding of the point at which such a marriage would be consummated).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">For starters, when the parent tells her child to go to her room, does the child obey or disobey? When she orders her child to, say, do his/ her chores... can the kid get out of it by summoning demons or elementals or the stalwart servitor?</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like you need examples that fit this setting more than something like a 20th century middle class suburban idea of parenting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Suddenly realizing that your daughter or son is an elemental demigod or chosen by the dragons, would mean a hell of a change in terms of discipline.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps. Again I feel that this is something that benefits more from trying to come with any one of a variety of specific scenarios rather than talking about broad trends.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I shudder to think what a teen who just realized that he'd been chosen by the dragons would lead to:<br /> <br /> Someone trying to live up to the expectations he had thrust upon him<br /> <br /> Or someone that's basically let the power go to his head.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> For a thing like this I'd suggest first coming up with what the home circumstances of the person are. Peasant farmer? Part of a craft trade family? Urban elite or urban poor?<br /> <br /> I would suggest that in many cases even with Exalting on the younger side, a pattern to the relationship has already been firmly established, for better or worse. I feel as though it would be most likely to be severely upended if the parents and child already had severely clashing personalities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens when you have to see the child you've raised since infancy, look at you with tears in their eyes and a light shining from them? Do they forsake everything they have in their world and go on the run</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's worth keeping in mind that for the vast majority of people in Creation, picking up and going on the run lies beyond their means. Immigration under such circumstances is difficult enough. Immigration while required to be alone and with a pursuit? Where are you going to spend the next several nights?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">do they just sit there and watch as their child disappears into the unknown?</div> </div> </div> </div>And this is actually an unexceptional circumstance anyway; it's going to be the case that many families that have multiple children and not enough property to distribute between them are going to have several of those children range out to try and find their own way, and in the absence of good infrastructure and widespread fast vehicles that trip typically goes one way. There is very often not going to be a private postal service, so when they depart that's probably the last you know of them. If it's a thing that many people are culturally conditioned to, and may well have already expected for the new Exalt, then it might not be so hard a disconnect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">When they stroll around and start building an empire, what place do they have for you?</div> </div> </div> </div>A nice villa on the hill and some good land for a retirement income?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T06:33:03-07:00","id":1380102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379527-exalts-with-dependents?p=1380091#post1380091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200b</span></span></span></div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Sometimes there is. Hopefully Dad will not pass away while you were seeking out the wizard whom you hoped would ensure he does not pass away while you're going out to find a peach of immortality.</span></span></span></div><br /> <br /> <br /> Do you know that that's a thing?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I know that its a thing. That's kinda why I suggested it. <br /> <br /> Yes, I know that. But at this point I'm presuming that if you're setting up an empire, you've known a wizard or two that would learn the spell as a favor to you (a favor owed by a solar exalt. Who wouldn't study their asses off for a few weeks to get the spell?)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379527-exalts-with-dependents?p=1380091#post1380091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> [COLOR=#252C2F][FONT=Helvetica][SIZE=13px]<div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200b</span></span></span></div>[LEFT]<br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">That said, an alternative path I considered is one in which the Exalted child wishes to go out and acquire a sudden surge of wealth to ensure an appropriately fine funeral to gird their parents for the world below. If they should fail, making a descent to try and strong arm a greater position for them directly is possible, and carries its own dramatic consequences. If a Deathlord or Abyssal reprimands you for such a defiance of the order of the Underworld, selfish and unfair to those who struggled to ensure that their lives would suitably garnish their deaths, are they in the wrong?</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> Maybe. Maybe not. <br /> <br /> But the tendency for any exalt with high virtues is to disagree, and say 'Maybe. But fuck that shit. My parents are going to have a nice un-life they didn't get in life.' and put out a kung fu duel underneath the underworld sky on the jade-black tiled roofs or something. <br /> <br /> </span></span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379527-exalts-with-dependents?p=1380091#post1380091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> [COLOR=#252C2F][FONT=Helvetica][SIZE=13px]<div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200b</span></span></span></div>[LEFT]<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I feel like you need examples that fit this setting more than something like a 20th century middle class suburban idea of parenting.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Perhaps. Again I feel that this is something that benefits more from trying to come with any one of a variety of specific scenarios rather than talking about broad trends.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Yes.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">For a thing like this I'd suggest first coming up with what the home circumstances of the person are. Peasant farmer? Part of a craft trade family? Urban elite or urban poor?</span></span></span><br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh no. Sorry. I guess I forgot to communicate that. I suppose that for this conversation, let's presume that one it's in a rural area, far from the urban centers, with a poorer and less well-off family. I'm actually thinking whether or not I should make her the widow, and then with a single son. Struggling day in and day out, working in the fields and whatever they could live off on the charity of their neighbours. <br /> <br /> Until her so exalts as a solar twilight, with a penchant for sorcery. That lasted for awhile. Long enough for their better luck to attract attention and basically force them to go on the run. Fortunately, the child has already started well enough grasp on their powers to get a few excellencies and charms. Enough to let them survive the first few nights.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T07:45:39-07:00","id":1380112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379527-exalts-with-dependents?p=1380102#post1380102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, I know that its a thing. That's kinda why I suggested it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You as a player might be aware, but not every <i>character's</i> going to know that it's actually <i>possible</i> for gods to uplift humans to divinity. They might live in an area without any legends of such, or even in places <i>with</i> those kinds of myths, might assume that it's just an allegory for Exaltation.<br /> <br /> \u200b&quot;How do you know that? Hey! I asked you a question. Did you read <i>Roll of Glorious Divinity I: Gods and Elementals</i>? Hey, what's that? What's that on the ground over there? Is that <i>Roll of Glorious Divinity I: Gods and Elementals?</i> How did that get there?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-10-2020, 10:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T08:04:36-07:00","id":1380120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379527-exalts-with-dependents?p=1380102#post1380102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, I know that its a thing. That's kinda why I suggested it.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I meant was that a character might be presumed to not be aware that humans can become gods. Indeed, I'd imagine that to be the default.<br /> <br /> I'll cop to a bias in discussions like this; if I perceive somebody to suggest things in terms of trying to devise an optimal solution to secure all contingencies, I'm liable to jump on it even if it should be valid among the many possibilities that a story might take.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, I know that. But at this point I'm presuming that if you're setting up an empire, you've known a wizard or two that would learn the spell as a favor to you (a favor owed by a solar exalt. Who wouldn't study their asses off for a few weeks to get the spell?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Devout Immaculates.<br /> <br /> That and people need sources for spells, devising them for oneself is implicitly harder.<br /> <br /> A wide enough network of contacts reliably catches sorcerers, as the Guild indicates, but I feel as though a spell such as that would be obscure. I'm not even sure it's Terrestrial Circle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the tendency for any exalt with high virtues is to disagree, and say 'Maybe. But fuck that shit. My parents are going to have a nice un-life they didn't get in life.' and put out a kung fu duel underneath the underworld sky on the jade-black tiled roofs or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some people might define virtue as incompatible with any of several points in that thought process. I'm ambivalent towards a perspective of Exalted as people who universally can and will place their own will above all other possibilities, especially when phrased as enforced with violence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose that for this conversation, let's presume that one it's in a rural area, far from the urban centers, with a poorer and less well-off family. I'm actually thinking whether or not I should make her the widow, and then with a single son. Struggling day in and day out, working in the fields and whatever they could live off on the charity of their neighbours. <br /> <br /> Until her so exalts as a solar twilight, with a penchant for sorcery. That lasted for awhile. Long enough for their better luck to attract attention and basically force them to go on the run. Fortunately, the child has already started well enough grasp on their powers to get a few excellencies and charms. Enough to let them survive the first few nights.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... I'm usually the last person to go with the idea that the Solar Exalted should be going for big things right at the start and at all times thereafter, but even I feel as though the start of this scenario is lacking something, some impetus for being Exalted and doing things with it. <br /> <br /> Buuutttt... hurdles that could be overcome with some specific details, moving on.<br /> <br /> I feel as though a scenario such as this is one where an immediate priority is to get one's parent into a secure environment before seeing to their own needs, because a continuous hard travel can take a bad toll on an older person even without the active pursuit of Wyld Hunt or the like. Assuming one is not setting up a tragedy.<br /> <br /> My first thought goes to a few nights roughing it in the wilderness before an emissary from the local spirit court approaches to offer sanctuary for the dependent as a gesture of good will in hopes of acquiring the Exalt's friendship.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T09:23:50-07:00","id":1380145,"title":"","content":"My Daybreak has two children and a husband. The husband is the critically ill mortal prince of Y'danna whose health is being sustained through a combination of her own magics and something her patron the Lover Clad is doing to help (but at what cost?)<br /> <br /> So she's currently away from them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T10:38:30-07:00","id":1380155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379527-exalts-with-dependents?p=1380145#post1380145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My Daybreak has two children and a husband. The husband is the critically ill mortal prince of Y'danna whose health is being sustained through a combination of her own magics and something her patron the Lover Clad is doing to help (but at what cost?)<br /> <br /> So she's currently away from them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any nice ruby furniture in the house?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T16:00:00-07:00","id":1380225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379527-exalts-with-dependents?p=1380155#post1380155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Any nice ruby furniture in the house?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't quite get this reference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T16:31:32-07:00","id":1380232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379527-exalts-with-dependents?p=1380225#post1380225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't quite get this reference.</div> </div> </div> </div>She's partially based on Elric of Melnibon\u00e9's love interest Cymoril. Specifically the most recent Titan Comics version who was keeping him alive through human sacrifice until he got his soul-stealing wifeklave Stormbringer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T10:01:14-07:00","id":1380405,"title":"","content":"This topic is concerned about Exalts with dependants, but I think there's also a potential and intertwined subject of interest for Exalts that <i>are</i> dependants, in a manner of speaking.<br /> <br /> I was just reading about the grisettes of Paris; young, single working class urban women of the first half of the 19th century. Economic necessity and social restrictions require them to work in the textile factories and as seamstresses and hatmakers and shop assistants by day, but by night they would go out into the world of the bohemians. Frequent the haunts of the subculture of artists and poets of various means, become their casual girlfriends at a time when this was still an unusual domestic arrangement, serving as models verging on something close to aspiring professional muses. They were women in absolutely terrible conditions who still found a standard to assert themselves and be part of a more culturally and intellectually engaging life.<br /> <br /> It reminded me of a character idea I had some time back, of a Zenith Caste Exalt who was something like one of the Great Beauties of China crossed with stories of the famed courtesans of Delhi by way of Helen of Troy. A woman of such beauty and character and insight and culture that so many who look upon her fall down in awe and want to hand her the world just for a passing touch of her favour. Who can look deep into people's souls and find what will give them comfort or the scorn that will shatter them, and they will become utterly dedicated for the privilege. She does not command, but it's not necessary to do so when the mighty gods and princes that surround her will bend all things as they suppose she wants in her direction.<br /> <br /> That's perhaps on the more extreme end of how such a thing can go, but I think there's good dramatic and interpersonal potential for the Exalt as a figure who cultivates devotion in others to inspire them to proactively see to all of their wishes and needs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T09:39:46-07:00","id":1381348,"title":"","content":"And another thing. Apologies if it's already said.<br /> <br /> I think there's potential for a story or exploration of the relationships when one of your children exalt. Like, put it like winning the lottery, or becoming the parent of a child star. One day, you're normal lady, waitress at the tri-forked inn. You work all day at the inn, serving meat buns and tea to passerbys. You live in a small town or city, where you and your child eke out a moderately comfortable life. Sometimes you get hungry, and the owner of the inn lets you take home some food for the day. You're frankly speaking, not all that wealthy, your husband having died a long time ago/ left you, and you owe it to your neighbours to watch over your son. You live in the poorer parts of town. Not that bad, but bad enough you feel worried while serving customers. Sometimes, the customers are rough, and you have to make sure they don't get too handsy. You don't get much traffic with the gods or the higher mortal authorities, and you pray that is all that happens. You pray to the gods, and you pay your taxes, and hope that you and your children pass the days uneventfully. <br /> <br /> And then one day, the news comes. Your son has, in an altercation with a rather abusive/ violent guard, had exalted as an Earth aspect, standing his ground to the abusive mortal. News has come out already. Yes, you have never wanted to stand out and be up and running in the higher affairs of the elites. Too bad. You're the mother of a dragonblooded exalt in an area which venerates the immaculate faith. You don't have a choice now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T13:02:22-07:00","id":1381410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379527-exalts-with-dependents?p=1381348#post1381348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And another thing. Apologies if it's already said.<br /> <br /> I think there's potential for a story or exploration of the relationships when one of your children exalt. Like, put it like winning the lottery, or becoming the parent of a child star. One day, you're normal lady, waitress at the tri-forked inn. You work all day at the inn, serving meat buns and tea to passerbys. You live in a small town or city, where you and your child eke out a moderately comfortable life. Sometimes you get hungry, and the owner of the inn lets you take home some food for the day. You're frankly speaking, not all that wealthy, your husband having died a long time ago/ left you, and you owe it to your neighbours to watch over your son. You live in the poorer parts of town. Not that bad, but bad enough you feel worried while serving customers. Sometimes, the customers are rough, and you have to make sure they don't get too handsy. You don't get much traffic with the gods or the higher mortal authorities, and you pray that is all that happens. You pray to the gods, and you pay your taxes, and hope that you and your children pass the days uneventfully. <br /> <br /> And then one day, the news comes. Your son has, in an altercation with a rather abusive/ violent guard, had exalted as an Earth aspect, standing his ground to the abusive mortal. News has come out already. Yes, you have never wanted to stand out and be up and running in the higher affairs of the elites. Too bad. You're the mother of a dragonblooded exalt in an area which venerates the immaculate faith. You don't have a choice now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Take your Script. Hand over the boy. Shut your mouth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T13:23:39-07:00","id":1381419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379527-exalts-with-dependents?p=1381410#post1381410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Take your Script. Hand over the boy. Shut your mouth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind you, this is out in the threshold, in a place were the immaculate faith exists and yet doesn't have all-encompassing power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T13:24:32-07:00","id":1381420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379527-exalts-with-dependents?p=1381410#post1381410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Take your Script. Hand over the boy. Shut your mouth.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the realm yes, and its satrapies perhaps. But what about in the Scavenger Lands?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T13:54:03-07:00","id":1381429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379527-exalts-with-dependents?p=1381420#post1381420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the realm yes, and its satrapies perhaps. But what about in the Scavenger Lands?</div> </div> </div> </div>Lookshy exists and recruits Dragon-Blooded too.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T14:59:43-07:00","id":1381447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379527-exalts-with-dependents?p=1381429#post1381429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lookshy exists and recruits Dragon-Blooded too.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Lookshy is in no position to conscript every outcaste in the Hundred Kingdoms. Hell, they are in no position to conscript almost any outcaste in the Hundred Kingdoms beyond those that exalt in Lookshy and its immediate environs. Recruit yes, conscript no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T15:07:28-07:00","id":1381449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379527-exalts-with-dependents?p=1381420#post1381420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the realm yes, and its satrapies perhaps. But what about in the Scavenger Lands?</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect you'd get people with wealth and power offering to help the kid out and/or find him gainful employment. A lot of people would very much like to have a new Exalt feeling indebted to them, or perhaps to get the kid to agree to work for (insert inadequate wage here) before he realizes how much he's really worth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T15:09:48-07:00","id":1381450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379527-exalts-with-dependents?p=1381447#post1381447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lookshy is in no position to conscript every outcaste in the Hundred Kingdoms. Hell, they are in no position to conscript almost any outcaste in the Hundred Kingdoms beyond those that exalt in Lookshy and its immediate environs. Recruit yes, conscript no.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even the Realm doesn't aggressively kidnap outcaste DBs. They do try to make the deal of joining up seem really sweet though. Set your family up really nice, lots of money, come live in luxury for the rest of your life with a stipend that you don't have to work for.<br /> <br /> If you want to turn that down a big problem will be your son killed a Dynast, so they might be looking to settle a score by at least getting another DB back for that. Or just settling a score in general. Another problem is if you ever flare your anima or something trying to kill recruiters, because now you're anathema who's kidnapped a poor lost egg. From the point of view of a Dynast or even a Lookshian that's particularly bad even for anathema.<br /> <br /> So you're probably going to want to keep your head down, and try to keep them away from the big terrestrial empires in a way that won't spark an even greater crusade for the both of you. Maybe go align yourself with some other independent kingdom somewhere. If you're writing a story or a running a campaign for that you could dodge between trying to stop your very young, essence-blood-burning child from acting out, dodging imperial recruiters or other local powers who would love a young, moldable exalt on their team, and pursuing any other goals you might have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T16:06:48-07:00","id":1381462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379527-exalts-with-dependents?p=1381447#post1381447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lookshy is in no position to conscript every outcaste in the Hundred Kingdoms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did I say &quot;conscript?&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200bJust double-checked - no. The word I chose was very specifically &quot;recruit.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T16:48:16-07:00","id":1381469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379527-exalts-with-dependents?p=1381348#post1381348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there's potential for a story or exploration of the relationships when one of your children exalt. Like, put it like winning the lottery, or becoming the parent of a child star. One day, you're normal lady, waitress at the tri-forked inn. You work all day at the inn, serving meat buns and tea to passerbys. You live in a small town or city, where you and your child eke out a moderately comfortable life. Sometimes you get hungry, and the owner of the inn lets you take home some food for the day. You're frankly speaking, not all that wealthy, your husband having died a long time ago/ left you, and you owe it to your neighbours to watch over your son. </div> </div> </div> </div>Well, keep in mind that in circumstances like what you're describing, in the economic realities of much of urban Creation, watching over your son means making sure that he's engaged in some form of work.<br /> <br /> Best case scenario for that is apprenticeship in... really, any trade at all is going to be lucky, even if it's one that is unpleasant and lacks prestige. Below that is &quot;unskilled&quot; labour, especially the kind that is best suited to somebody small and quick: running messages, hauling cargo, cleaning gutters and chimneys, picking up animal dung from the streets, that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> But that sort of thing has a tendency to be day labour, and will likely leave the kid with long stretches of free time. And that invariably means involvement in a gang, if only to get protection from the other gangs. That's a lot of time loitering and posturing, punctuated with short bursts of vandalism, petty theft and getting into brawls with the other gangs over turf, feuds or just to burn off some energy.<br /> <br /> And keep in mind, of they're not in an apprenticeship or some form of schooling, involvement in some kind of gang is basically inevitable for urban kids of a certain age.<br /> <br /> That kid Exalts? Your first concern is that his profile within the gang is going to rise, drawing the allegiance of admirers and sycophants even if he doesn't start acquiring them through violence. But violence is likely to come up if there's any ambition or pressure from anybody between the gang's still reigning leader (whom you can't possibly oust, you owe him everything) to the toadies to the new bed mate. Voices saying that you actually finally have the muscle to own this town. Beat all the other gangs into submission, take what you please from the smaller wholesalers and use the proceeds to live the high life with the businesses tough enough to not roll over for some lone Exalt. People here are Immaculates? Great, you can pass over throwing this weight around as your right for service in a past life.<br /> <br /> You're his mother, maybe you feel some obligation to impose a moral standard on him, but next thing you know you're getting gifts of silk gowns, balsam perfumes and pearl necklaces (so long as you don't ask where they came from). From now on you're the one being waited on, and in more upscale joints than where you used to work. People who literally spat on you a year ago now start bowing their heads and scraping aside when your sedan chair passes by.<br /> <br /> Are you sure you <i>want</i> to rein him in?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T00:19:44-07:00","id":1381545,"title":"","content":"I admit that I\u2019m thinking of Crow the Boy\u2019s backstory now, for all that she and her gang were all orphans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T00:53:42-07:00","id":1381557,"title":"","content":"Can imagine a scenario where the parents \u2013 if they are both are around and of the right age \u2013 are intensively interrogated about their genealogy and put on something like a retainer (obviously a simple tryst with a wandering DB changes things).<br /> <br /> They've produced one Exalt, might they produce another? Might their relatives? Any (much) younger siblings would potentially get monitored as well - albeit the 'leftover child' info in WFHW makes it unlikely.<br /> <br /> Sort of pro-sport style youth scouting/tapping up, but with magic elemental powers. DB 'recruitment agent' might be an interesting idea for a character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","user":"Moss Reynholm","date":". 04-15-2020, 04:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T01:13:47-07:00","id":1381560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379527-exalts-with-dependents?p=1381419#post1381419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind you, this is out in the threshold, in a place were the immaculate faith exists and yet doesn't have all-encompassing power.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's worth noting they're more manipulative about it than that response may indicate.<br /> <br /> If he gets adopted he'll have access to a better standard of education than you could possibly afford and they'll probably pay her enough to buy a much nicer inn than the one she's working in.<br /> However, it's very unlikely that she'll ever see her son again not because of any coercion but because the Immaculate religion is going to be used to remind both mother and son that they live in very different worlds now and that it's probably for the best that she doesn't visit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T02:53:13-07:00","id":1381577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379527-exalts-with-dependents?p=1381557#post1381557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can imagine a scenario where the parents \u2013 if they are both are around and of the right age \u2013 are intensively interrogated about their genealogy and put on something like a retainer (obviously a simple tryst with a wandering DB changes things).<br /> <br /> They've produced one Exalt, might they produce another? Might their relatives? Any (much) younger siblings would potentially get monitored as well - albeit the 'leftover child' info in WFHW makes it unlikely.<br /> <br /> Sort of pro-sport style youth scouting/tapping up, but with magic elemental powers. DB 'recruitment agent' might be an interesting idea for a character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Think about it. Its worse than that. <br /> <br /> There's a webcomic. Strong Female Protagonist. The titular character is an expy of superman. Capable of pushing her way through a mountain. Capable of shrugging off artillery shells. She's only been wounded twice. When she goes for a haircut, the barber uses diamond saw blades which have to be replaced every 4 minutes, because the act of cutting her hair already wears them down to uselessness.She is the household name for superpowers, world-famous, and the pentagon has plans for what to do when she goes rogue (a fleet of spaceships)<br /> <br /> She has a sister. It works out exactly as well as you think it would. <br /> <br /> It would be the ultimate trump card to bring out at family reunions. What happens when you are joe mortal, and then your brother isn't just a big time lawyer or financier, but an elemental demigod who is going to live centuries and make the universe shake with his footsteps? What happens when you live your entire life, knowing you'll never be as good as your cousin/ brother? What happens when you see your parents watch you, praying every night as you grow up, only for those looks of hope to turn into disappointment as you grow to 21 years old with no spark of exaltation. What happens when you know. Not think. Know, that you'll die in the dirt as a mortal, when some quirk of fate had exalted your sibling as a superhuman elemental bodhisattva taht is the pinnacle of spiritual enlightenment. <br /> <br /> Worse if its a younger brother that exalted. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5Weaop_aiTg\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5Weaop_aiTg\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5Weaop_aiTg\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5Weaop_aiTg </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T03:33:03-07:00","id":1381588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379527-exalts-with-dependents?p=1381545#post1381545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admit that I\u2019m thinking of Crow the Boy\u2019s backstory now, for all that she and her gang were all orphans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, kids in that situation have a different tone to them when there work becomes a matter of actual survival rather than limited occupation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379527-exalts-with-dependents?p=1381557#post1381557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can imagine a scenario where the parents \u2013 if they are both are around and of the right age \u2013 are intensively interrogated about their genealogy and put on something like a retainer (obviously a simple tryst with a wandering DB changes things).<br /> <br /> They've produced one Exalt, might they produce another? Might their relatives? Any (much) younger siblings would potentially get monitored as well - albeit the 'leftover child' info in WFHW makes it unlikely.<br /> <br /> Sort of pro-sport style youth scouting/tapping up, but with magic elemental powers. DB 'recruitment agent' might be an interesting idea for a character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehhh. The setting has always been written as though a sizable number of outcastes come out of nowhere, I think it's reasonable to expect most authorities in the setting to recognise that some random person Exalting is a complete fluke. Additional siblings Exalting might not be completely impossible, but so vanishingly unlikely that it's absurd to bet on it.<br /> <br /> Besides, what is interrogation likely to reveal? Are these poor people experts in their own genealogy? At best there might be a family almanac or something. Otherwise, if that information exists at all it's probably kept elsewhere.<br /> <br /> Unless this is conducted for dramatic purposes by people that are jerks, at the direction of a storyteller who is aware that it's fruitless.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379527-exalts-with-dependents?p=1381577#post1381577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Think about it. Its worse than that. <br /> <br /> There's a webcomic. Strong Female Protagonist. The titular character is an expy of superman. Capable of pushing her way through a mountain. Capable of shrugging off artillery shells. She's only been wounded twice. When she goes for a haircut, the barber uses diamond saw blades which have to be replaced every 4 minutes, because the act of cutting her hair already wears them down to uselessness.She is the household name for superpowers, world-famous, and the pentagon has plans for what to do when she goes rogue (a fleet of spaceships)<br /> <br /> She has a sister. It works out exactly as well as you think it would. <br /> <br /> It would be the ultimate trump card to bring out at family reunions. What happens when you are joe mortal, and then your brother isn't just a big time lawyer or financier, but an elemental demigod who is going to live centuries and make the universe shake with his footsteps? What happens when you live your entire life, knowing you'll never be as good as your cousin/ brother? What happens when you see your parents watch you, praying every night as you grow up, only for those looks of hope to turn into disappointment as you grow to 21 years old with no spark of exaltation. What happens when you know. Not think. Know, that you'll die in the dirt as a mortal, when some quirk of fate had exalted your sibling as a superhuman elemental bodhisattva taht is the pinnacle of spiritual enlightenment. <br /> <br /> Worse if its a younger brother that exalted. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5Weaop_aiTg\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5Weaop_aiTg\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5Weaop_aiTg\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5Weaop_aiTg </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Could try their hand at the Guild. See if Exalted sibling can hook them up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T04:02:53-07:00","id":1381599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379527-exalts-with-dependents?p=1381577#post1381577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Think about it. Its worse than that.<br /> <br /> There's a webcomic. Strong Female Protagonist. The titular character is an expy of superman. Capable of pushing her way through a mountain. Capable of shrugging off artillery shells. She's only been wounded twice. When she goes for a haircut, the barber uses diamond saw blades which have to be replaced every 4 minutes, because the act of cutting her hair already wears them down to uselessness.She is the household name for superpowers, world-famous, and the pentagon has plans for what to do when she goes rogue (a fleet of spaceships)<br /> <br /> She has a sister. It works out exactly as well as you think it would.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Aaaaand just ploughed through about 45 pages and counting of awesome instead of doing what I should be doing. Thanks <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12952\" data-vbnamecard=\"12952\">Accelerator</a>...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T04:41:46-07:00","id":1381604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379527-exalts-with-dependents?p=1381588#post1381588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Could try their hand at the Guild. See if Exalted sibling can hook them up.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's even worse. <br /> <br /> *points to video*<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T05:37:01-07:00","id":1381615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379527-exalts-with-dependents?p=1381604#post1381604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*points to video*</div> </div> </div> </div>What does The Godfather Part 2 have to do with the Guild?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T06:20:36-07:00","id":1381626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379527-exalts-with-dependents?p=1381615#post1381615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does The Godfather Part 2 have to do with the Guild?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because I'm saying that having a sibling as an exalt would likely engender great amounts of inferiority in any person, and having the exalt help him get a position at the guild wouldn't help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T06:46:12-07:00","id":1381633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379527-exalts-with-dependents?p=1381626#post1381626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because I'm saying that having a sibling as an exalt would likely engender great amounts of inferiority in any person...</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know that I'd extend that to &quot;<i>any</i> person&quot; - I'm sure there's more than zero that would just be happy for their sibling.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379527-exalts-with-dependents?p=1381626#post1381626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...and having the exalt help him get a position at the guild wouldn't help.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, that's gonna depend on the person and their worldview. A person with a Defining Principle of &quot;Always remember that we're all in this together&quot; is probably not going to be all that broken up by having needed help once.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T11:44:39-07:00","id":1381720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379527-exalts-with-dependents?p=1381626#post1381626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because I'm saying that having a sibling as an exalt would likely engender great amounts of inferiority in any person, and having the exalt help him get a position at the guild wouldn't help.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fredo's problem was not that he did not shine when set beside Michael, his problem was that he sucked no matter where you put him.<br /> <br /> Hey Fredo, maybe actually lay some groundwork for building up the new business in Vegas without becoming Moe Greene's lackey before you start pitifully whinging about your lack of responsibilities and respect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-16T15:37:09-07:00","id":1381999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379527-exalts-with-dependents?p=1381577#post1381577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a webcomic. Strong Female Protagonist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Slight derail:<br /> <br /> That was a very disappointing webcomic. I'd hoped it'd explore the themes we're discussing here beyond Kylo Ren screaming &quot;I hate you!&quot; Then Mary Sue responding &quot;I know.&quot; Mega Girl may as well not have a family.<br /> <br /> And it starts so well. The exact moment it fell apart from me was (not the whole disappointing lack of any meaningful storytelling with the resentful sister, but) Issue 5 Page 33 when it felt like I was reading the &quot;Is my character a Mary Sue&quot; Quiz in comic book form.<br /> <br /> Still... good fodder for Exalted stories played as power fantasies. Lots of stealable elements around what to do if you're too powerful. I especially liked Issue 7s ending for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T02:37:13-07:00","id":1382090,"title":"","content":"Oh great. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7\" data-vbnamecard=\"7\">Lioness</a>, question. Does the forum always eat up posts? Is there a way to restore them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T03:01:14-07:00","id":1382096,"title":"","content":"There's a few ways that posts could be &quot;eaten&quot; by forum software. Sometimes if you have lots of links in your post or an IP address the forum software deems suspicious posts get caught in the spam filter until a moderator approves them but if your session is timing out before you're posting there's not a lot that can be done about it.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T04:46:14-07:00","id":1382121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379527-exalts-with-dependents?p=1382096#post1382096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a few ways that posts could be &quot;eaten&quot; by forum software. Sometimes if you have lots of links in your post or an IP address the forum software deems suspicious posts get caught in the spam filter until a moderator approves them but if your session is timing out before you're posting there's not a lot that can be done about it.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, goddamn-.... <br /> <br /> Crap. I'll just rewrite the entire post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T05:19:23-07:00","id":1382127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379527-exalts-with-dependents?p=1381999#post1381999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Slight derail:<br /> <br /> That was a very disappointing webcomic. I'd hoped it'd explore the themes we're discussing here beyond Kylo Ren screaming &quot;I hate you!&quot; Then Mary Sue responding &quot;I know.&quot; Mega Girl may as well not have a family.<br /> <br /> And it starts so well. The exact moment it fell apart from me was (not the whole disappointing lack of any meaningful storytelling with the resentful sister, but) Issue 5 Page 33 when it felt like I was reading the &quot;Is my character a Mary Sue&quot; Quiz in comic book form.<br /> <br /> Still... good fodder for Exalted stories played as power fantasies. Lots of stealable elements around what to do if you're too powerful. I especially liked Issue 7s ending for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Link?<br /> <br /> 2. Back on the family thing...<br /> <br /> What if you're in a village, far from the threshold, or even any whiff of the immaculate faith? Your villagers get up, go to work the fields, pray in the evening, then go back to bed. They hope that no horrible wolves come around, or fair folk, or bandits, or behemoths would wander out of the wyld. Their greatest weapon is a rusty knife tied to a stick. There are barely any stone buildings there, most of the things made of mud or wood. Nothing happens there... until one of them exalts. Maybe a guardsmen. Or maybe a priest or aspiring shaman or medicine woman that carried out some incredible feat of genius. Either way, now the solar is a person, is a pillar of the community that cannot leave, and most likely has strong bonds to the community. <br /> <br /> So now you can't move, because they've already put roots there. And besides, these guys would have to move at the speed of the slowest moving person. In other words, they're your community in a dangerous world where death can come at any minute. Thus, you have to defend them. From everything.<br /> <br /> Farming is revolutionalized by new farming techniques, seeds, machinery, and bargains with the neighbouring gods and elementals. The earth is warped, forming ditches, irrigation, walls, roads, kill-zones, and fortress cities. Medicine is transformed. No one dies of infections and bleeding out and any curable diseases, and medicine for smooth pregnancies is available for free. The great leader needs more people for his grand plans. Warriors now march in closed ranks of burnished steel, the scattered formation and rusty weapons a thing of the past. Children born after this listen to stories of their elders of famine during the winter or of great plagues with ill-disguised ignorance, never knowing anything other than comfort and hospitable weather.<br /> <br /> I think I went on to a large tangent there, but basically, an extremely driven and dedicated solar/ lunar can probably cause an incredible change seemingly-overnight (from the point of view of geopolitics). <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T06:03:38-07:00","id":1382140,"title":"","content":"That's how the writer of the 2nd edition Bull's Empire looked at it; scattered raiders turned into an efficient professional military, nomads turned into rulers of cities, veneration of animals turned into spirit pacts and Sun-worship. The old men and women looking uneasy at their grandchildren drilling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T04:49:56-07:00","id":1382495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379527-exalts-with-dependents?p=1382127#post1382127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So now you can't move, because they've already put roots there. And besides, these guys would have to move at the speed of the slowest moving person. In other words, they're your community in a dangerous world where death can come at any minute. Thus, you have to defend them. From everything.<br /> <br /> Farming is revolutionalized by new farming techniques, seeds, machinery, and bargains with the neighbouring gods and elementals. The earth is warped, forming ditches, irrigation, walls, roads, kill-zones, and fortress cities. Medicine is transformed. No one dies of infections and bleeding out and any curable diseases, and medicine for smooth pregnancies is available for free. The great leader needs more people for his grand plans. Warriors now march in closed ranks of burnished steel, the scattered formation and rusty weapons a thing of the past. Children born after this listen to stories of their elders of famine during the winter or of great plagues with ill-disguised ignorance, never knowing anything other than comfort and hospitable weather.<br /> I think I went on to a large tangent there, but basically, an extremely driven and dedicated solar/ lunar can probably cause an incredible change seemingly-overnight (from the point of view of geopolitics).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, sure, one <i>extremely</i> dedicated exalt, or a circle with a proper complement of roles.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T05:15:22-07:00","id":1382499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379527-exalts-with-dependents?p=1382495#post1382495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, sure, one <i>extremely</i> dedicated exalt, or a circle with a proper complement of roles.</div> </div> </div> </div>I should put up a thread. <br /> <br /> Asking 'how much infrastructure building have you guys done with a circle'?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T05:40:23-07:00","id":1382503,"title":"","content":"That might be kind of interesting. My guess is that it varies massively.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T06:14:07-07:00","id":1382507,"title":"","content":"A Dragon-Blooded Dynast might have her husband (if he\u2019s not Exalted too) and maybe her kids as dependents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T08:35:41-07:00","id":1382533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379527-exalts-with-dependents?p=1382507#post1382507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Dragon-Blooded Dynast might have her husband (if he\u2019s not Exalted too) and maybe her kids as dependents.</div> </div> </div> </div>The <i>default</i> is that Dynast Exalts have one child every decade or two, and are unlikely to take this family unit off the Blessed Isle even if on a long term assignment.<br /> <br /> But, well, the campaign might be set on the Isle, or the character might have <i>started</i> a family off the Isle for various reasons.<br /> <br /> Also, it need not necessary be a husband <i>per se</i>, and adopted stepchildren or such are possible too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 04-19-2020, 11:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T13:01:37-07:00","id":1382576,"title":"","content":"Interesting. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T06:03:51-07:00","id":1382727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379527-exalts-with-dependents?p=1382533#post1382533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The <i>default</i> is that Dynast Exalts have one child every decade or two, and <b>are unlikely to take this family unit off the Blessed Isle</b> even if on a long term assignment.<br /> <br /> But, well, the campaign might be set on the Isle, or the character might have <i>started</i> a family off the Isle for various reasons.<br /> <br /> Also, it need not necessary be a husband <i>per se</i>, and adopted stepchildren or such are possible too.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you can modify armor to breastfeed your baby on the battlefield, you can take your kid's Patrician tutors to your palace on the Threshold.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T10:39:58-07:00","id":1382795,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar531_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"531\" data-vbnamecard=\"531\">JohnDoe244</a> very true \ud83d\ude0a","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T12:41:39-07:00","id":1382809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379527-exalts-with-dependents?p=1380002#post1380002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great for battle groups, but doesn't do anything exceptional for individuals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right.<br /> <br /> I think Tiger-Warrior Training Technique has become &quot;teach mortals how to fight as a coordinated unit&quot;, like the Spartan shield-wall or the Macedonian phalanx. Skills which are absolutely useless for an individual fighting alone, while still being amazingly effective for an assembled cohort.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T01:25:13-07:00","id":1382924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379527-exalts-with-dependents?p=1382727#post1382727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you can modify armor to breastfeed your baby on the battlefield, you can take your kid's Patrician tutors to your palace on the Threshold.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, possibly as Dynasts are more involved in child rearing this edition, and I guess, particularly with rising nervousness about the succession crisis. <br /> <br /> Hmm... So , yeah...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 04-21-2020, 04:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T05:11:44-07:00","id":1382958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379527-exalts-with-dependents?p=1382924#post1382924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, possibly as Dynasts are more involved in child rearing this edition, and I guess, particularly with rising nervousness about the succession crisis. <br /> <br /> Hmm... So , yeah...</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think they're any more involved this edition to others. (The armor thing is from MoeP<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />B if memory serves.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T07:19:05-07:00","id":1382970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379527-exalts-with-dependents?p=1382958#post1382958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think they're any more involved this edition to others. (The armor thing is from MoeP<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />B if memory serves.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say the default presentation is <i>marginally</i> improved, from uninterested at all, to distant but loving.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoEP : DB 18</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The state-sponsored hardening of a Dynast into a Dragon-Blooded soldier starts almost immediately. Dynastic children are handed over to wet nurses within moments of their birth lest they form an inappropriate bond with their mothers. Infancy is spent among young, un-Exalted women of the household and nurses who attend to their every need. Few parents find their children particularly interesting until they Exalt, and most are happy to remain well away from their progeny until they prove that they\u2019re worth speaking to.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WFHW99</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dragon-Blooded parents are typically cold, distant, and rarely there. Many children grow up knowing their tutors and servants better than their own parents. This is normal in the Realm, but it doesn\u2019t mean that the Dragon-Blooded don\u2019t love their children. The greatest gifts a loving mother can pass on to her daughter are a strong house and a respected lineage \u2014 the memory of a mother\u2019s voice simply cannot outweigh pragmatic concerns.<br /> To sacrifice relationships with children is considered a solemn and melancholy duty in the Dynasty, and is most commendable. It\u2019s a common topic of poems and songs, often ending with the satisfied parent realizing it was all worth it when she sees her child benefit from her hard work in adulthood. Most Dragon-Blooded parents make this sacrifice, but not all. Those who don\u2019t are considered lazy or self-indulgent. That said, Exalted parents \u2014 having passed along the Dragon\u2019s blood \u2014 have no further responsibility to their children beyond necessities and tutelage.</div> </div> </div> </div>But as always, the metric varies.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 04-21-2020, 10:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T08:27:01-07:00","id":1382974,"title":"","content":"Now now, let's not get begged down in all of the details of how terrible Manual of Exalted Power: Dragon Blooded was, hehehehe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379527-exalts-with-dependents?p=1382958#post1382958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(The armor thing is from MoeP: DB if memory serves.)</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be in the backstory of Tepet Ejava as originally told in Aspect Book: Wood and repeated in Scroll of Exalts.<br /> <br /> Really, even that exceptional circumstance is not a concern, as What Fire Has Wrought mentions that there are a few primary schools in the satrapies to service any large enough Dynast populations or the cadet Houses. I think nothing about the usual standards of Dynast child rearing precludes the idea that making one's residence in the Threshold entails having one's children in the household until they reach school age, although I'd expect even then the preference is to send them back to the Blessed Isle for their education. Heck, even in cases where their being sent to a closer academy (or even home schooling) is the first option, there can be exigencies behind that other than being one of those weirdos who's more personally affectionate with your children. I imagine bringing them up with an intention of them being able to effectively operate and have connections in the Threshold is a significant concern to some.<br /> <br /> Really, if the child has not yet been sent off to boarding school, both of the parents being absent from supervising their upbringing seems to me far more like a stigma among Dynast society; ensuring that your children are brought up correctly is a sacred duty to House, empire and Creation itself. What kind of dilettante are you to pawn it off on another? <br /> <br /> That said, cadet Houses are an alternative recourse for the Dynastic lifestyle out in a riskier environment.<br /> <br /> Actually, wait, why was the point about whether or not Dynastic children are brought off of the Blessed Isle brought up in the first place? They don't need to be in danger to be dependents. They don't need to be off the Blessed Isle to be in danger; those kids are expected to know how to apply life-saving first aid to one another, what does that tell you?<br /> <br /> Just kind of came out of nowhere...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-18T00:59:26-07:00","id":1414336,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure if I've posted this here before, but I&quot;m going to post it. <br /> <br /> Marriage. With children. At the age of 20-21. <br /> <br /> And then, Dragonblooded Exaltation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-18T01:45:30-07:00","id":1414338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1379527-exalts-with-dependents?p=1414336#post1414336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure if I've posted this here before, but I&amp;quot;m going to post it. <br /> <br /> Marriage. With children. At the age of 20-21. <br /> <br /> And then, Dragonblooded Exaltation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean... It's unlikely.<br /> <br /> Marriage, with children, at age 19, and then, Dragon-Blooded Exaltation seems more likely.<br /> <br /> In the Realm that's a recipe for heartbreak. Join the Legions and never see your family grow up? Become Immaculate? You're too old for adoption.<br /> <br /> On the Threshold... VtM had a section about Cleavers in the Time of Thin Blood supplement. I kinda feel it probably goes like that. <br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> Whilst I'm here...<br /> <br /> One of my PCs has a Defining Intimacy to their (adult) kids (who are Retainers), who they <i>basically</i> sent off to kill a Deathknight. I don't think it's apropos to just kill the kids off, out-of-hand (that definitely seems like a OOC conversation). But I also don't think they should waltz out of this concequence free. AITA if they come home missing an arm, or get taken prisoner or something?<br /> <br /> Session 0, we had a conversation about the level of plot armor Merit dots will get so it seems cut-and-dry to me. But then... this is a six page thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-18T03:12:30-07:00","id":1414344,"title":"","content":"My Twilight Crafter has a dad and 5 siblings, who are doing allright by farmer standards. His sisters are married off, his brother works the farm and has kids of his own. Young Salazan was discover to be a natural at smithing and so his dad apprenticed him out during a famine. <br /> <br /> Salazan hasn't seen any of them in 20 years, but now that he's filthy rich and technically the Duke/Jarl/Daimyo/whatever of their home province he's planning on seeing them soon. He's been sending them money for years to help out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-18T15:16:12-07:00","id":1414479,"title":"","content":"Leto and the Monsoon Dancer had dependents. Their solution was quite patrician: hire help. in their case people they trusted implicitly.<br /> The silver witch had kids basically every other year. That game was mostly centered on the colony our characters founded, so they quite literally just grew at home and had a weird mom that disappeared for a few months at a time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-26T10:24:05-07:00","id":1441523,"title":"","content":"Someone recently &quot;liked&quot; my post here, which makes me want to update how my game with dependents is going.<br /> <br /> The dependents in my game didn't really work out. We baby-yoda'd Reya's kid around in a custom-built baby carriage for a few sessions, which was fun. Hired an NPC baby sitter. Let the baby's mother play one of the major NPCs for some of the high danger scenes (I don't actually put my PCs in danger, but in-character it often feels like they're in danger). It was fun.<br /> <br /> A real kid, you don't get to give back when you're done with them. It's not a plot element that you can sideline. But in an RPG?<br /> <br /> We swapped STs, retired the mother to raise the kid off-screen for a bit and I'm playing the absentee father. The kids are very much off-screen and my character hasn't seen his youngest in over a year.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}